<title>GERMANY: Villeroy sees better 1997 after charge.</title>
<headline>Villeroy sees better 1997 after charge.</headline>
<dateline>METTLACH, Germany 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tableware and bathroom fittings group Villeroy &amp; Boch AG said on Wednesday it had a positive outlook on 1997 after taking a 114.1 million mark charge on its 1996 results as part of a restructuring.</p>
<p>Villeroy said it did not expect to face further charges in 1997 or 1998 and that it would start to reap the benefits of its restructuring programme with a &quot;clear profit improvement&quot; for the current business year.</p>
<p>The group said its products were well-received at international trade fairs in early 1997 and that its tableware and tiles groups reported higher sales in the first quarter over year-ago levels.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
